{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/InviteDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:02:20.885341Z","id":"1001bc9803945a25411738180887d1ebdab3e23dd9057317de5ddffe31c39725","body":{"detail":"POST /api/people/invites takes {viewer} (spec section 6.2), but the dialog offers only a new person or the owner's own machine. Naming a new person after a viewer who was never invited is 409 name_taken, whose message says to invite that viewer, which People cannot do yet. A viewer picker would use GET /api/viewers?q=.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":66},"end":{"line":67},"content_hash":"5aed600e45e79d959736f2f8b5fad319e35a36576ba1a9b733b99cfe892345cf"},"summary":"No invite for an existing LAN viewer","supersedes":"534d258c6a99631ed7bf6f45245ba08b45abe8e0d7b5a64cd970d871bae90729","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/People.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:02:20.886060Z","id":"4f66d956d05b45ed610223f45109389a3cc64d029db8a13fd4c0037722835290","body":{"detail":"People lists pending requests with Deny and links to the inbox for Approve; the approve form (code, new name, preset) is the inbox's connection card, which plan Task 21 builds (web/shell/src/people/ConnectionCard.svelte). Until then the inbox shows the request but cannot approve it from the shell.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":144},"end":{"line":144},"content_hash":"6a6b23888f43df54bf7304ec4eb8761e91735497209e0e4775466d231db404a7"},"summary":"Connection requests are approved in the inbox, not on People","supersedes":"cbce4d8bdb806b2f9030e911c2cd2a2e229ac4d454ea05a30509bf050475698c","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:02:20.886686Z","id":"d9c7672405a3113bea7e8664d0b72679c446253cbd106d534da3e9da67f5156a","body":{"detail":"raiseCaps tests the unraised rights at the artifact's ID, and an `own` location never covers a bare artifact ID (narrowerOrEqual's within). People does not know which artifacts are the person's (the artifact list carries no creator person), so for a Collaborator's agent 'Publish new versions' and 'Delete artifacts' at one of the person's own artifacts show unchecked and raisable. Raising there adds nothing the agent lacked; it only says less than it could. Fixing it needs the artifacts' person in GET /api/artifacts or a per-artifact rights check route.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":140},"end":{"line":157},"content_hash":"2920b50211feb7bfd4fc12cf7f96d2345f50abb8a6b0e84b4167a6d1e2dc53df"},"summary":"A raise at one of the person's own artifacts shows as not held","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/PersonCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:02:20.887393Z","id":"78560dd6d7f4509d046ad133a6563e378d0cd0797bcbb7d12d9b567a2171b6af","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e346be1d","summary":"Approval views carry artifact_title (8b8a8051), and approval rows say 'Allowed on “<title>”' or 'Allowed in one thread on “<title>”' (e346be1d). Evidence: PersonCard.test.ts 'names an approval's page when the daemon names it' passes; integration test approvals_name_the_owner_as_such_and_their_page asserts artifact_title 'Quarterly Review'.","supersedes":"2a0f0513adaefb7d58fac0a83843b3943f421eb1b1b53beef2ca5eb35dfd3f3c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:02:20.888050Z","id":"1bb5828a4bdd86518362febb7c60c363a91960b192a373af2754852ec51733b7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e346be1d","summary":"People's raise panel now takes a place, every artifact or one artifact from the live list, and counts an action as held only where the unraised rights allow it there. Evidence: model.test.ts 'counts an action as held only where the agent's rights allow it, so a Collaborator's agent can be raised to publish versions' and PersonCard.test.ts 'raises a Collaborator's agent to publish versions of one artifact' pass; e2e/people.spec.ts raises Sam's agent at one artifact and reads elevate [{type: clax-artifacts, actions: [update], locations: [<id>]}] from GET /api/people.","supersedes":"9b37d8dce5820c899da52cf299a93663649f27a8c6418a23c977dea3bd3d52e6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/InviteDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.164970Z","id":"7519ac056bc8df461d5a3df7a41594fcfae082a4a7ed907afecfd183ec6ecf88","body":{"detail":"POST /api/people/invites takes {viewer} (spec section 6.2), but the dialog offers only a new person or the owner's own machine. Naming a new person after a viewer who was never invited is 409 name_taken, whose message says to invite that viewer, which People cannot do yet. A viewer picker would use GET /api/viewers?q=.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":75},"end":{"line":76},"content_hash":"5aed600e45e79d959736f2f8b5fad319e35a36576ba1a9b733b99cfe892345cf"},"summary":"No invite for an existing LAN viewer","supersedes":"1001bc9803945a25411738180887d1ebdab3e23dd9057317de5ddffe31c39725","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/People.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.167374Z","id":"c819019969a294866a5bb1d07c1dba5094d684ed7fde22cef3fb9e2074cd6d3e","body":{"detail":"People lists pending requests with Deny and links to the inbox for Approve; the approve form (code, new name, preset) is the inbox's connection card, which plan Task 21 builds (web/shell/src/people/ConnectionCard.svelte). Until then the inbox shows the request but cannot approve it from the shell.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":152},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"6a6b23888f43df54bf7304ec4eb8761e91735497209e0e4775466d231db404a7"},"summary":"Connection requests are approved in the inbox, not on People","supersedes":"4f66d956d05b45ed610223f45109389a3cc64d029db8a13fd4c0037722835290","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/People.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:46:43.166253Z","id":"b714cf82b695aa82d6ba568c91acfba8af3a5186a181207c3f81361488bb95bd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9cfb85d5","span":{"start":{"line":144},"end":{"line":144},"content_hash":"399219efcda16cc7dbd6bca66609f58287688c0ce278c5e4134220f124177d6e"},"summary":"The inbox's connection card approves a request with its code, a new person's name and a preset (web/shell/src/people/ConnectionCard.svelte). Evidence: npx vitest run shell/src/people/ConnectionCard.test.ts passes ('enables Approve only with a typed code and a name for the new person, and approves with both and the preset'), and npx playwright test e2e/inbox-cards.spec.ts passes, Kim's clax connect finishing after the owner approves in the inbox.","supersedes":"4f66d956d05b45ed610223f45109389a3cc64d029db8a13fd4c0037722835290","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/ApprovalCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:48:04.741455Z","id":"5d149ae5227939920d701dd126c632ad885b6717ecdb226f2917daf667553180","body":{"detail":"Failure: a request whose comment has 3 lines of about 145 characters each (or 1-3 lines that together wrap past 3 visual lines, each under 160 characters). `long` (line 56) is false, since there are not more than 3 logical lines and none is over 160 characters, so no Show all button renders, while `.acard .held:not([data-open]) .htext` (line 120) clamps to 3 visual lines. Measured in Chromium on a scratch daemon: the card's .htext had scrollHeight > clientHeight with no .show button at both 1280 and 390 px; line 2 ended in an ellipsis and line 3 was invisible, before and after deciding. The approver decides without being able to read the withheld content (spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md §9.5, §26 (d)). No test covers it: deleting the 160-character clause leaves web/shell/src/people/ApprovalCard.test.ts passing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":55},"end":{"line":56},"content_hash":"8750c5fa6f86baf5eb6681800c5e9c7b4f459c1ffd0bf16a2b2778e5c336c5ec"},"suggested_fix":"Decide Show all from the rendered box (scrollHeight > clientHeight after layout, rechecked on resize), or clamp by logical lines only and let each shown line wrap in full; add a test with three long lines.","summary":"Withheld content is clipped with no Show all when its first lines wrap: the 3-line CSS clamp hides text that `long` does not count","tags":["review","task:21","severity:important","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/ApprovalCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:16:17.628851Z","id":"451d78f4f5dc3c9ef9c97f9ecb8e1016d107fe75a92917d078acf5fe73ef2197","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a5019f38","span":{"start":{"line":55},"end":{"line":56},"content_hash":"68d97ba458fd2380edbd5c0f7f9f5f77cd1481cadc4f197a37f2c0b64a2f02f9"},"summary":"Show all now follows the clamped text's laid-out box (scrollHeight beyond clientHeight), measured after each render and on every resize. Evidence: ApprovalCard.test.ts 'offers Show all when 3 lines wrap past the clamp, measured from the laid-out box, and again on resize' passes, and fails with `long` reduced to the line count; in Chromium a comment of three 145-character lines reads clipped=true showAll=true at 1280 and 390 px, light and dark (target/t21/shots-r1/person-approval-3x145-*).","supersedes":"5d149ae5227939920d701dd126c632ad885b6717ecdb226f2917daf667553180","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:12:47.352509Z","id":"9a2e1d3366a4adbb9dfbffa1fc0b055e9f42d4d40f4b2184df55a51d6da28475","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:665a0447","summary":"The line now says each agent has its own credential, so its limits hold against other agents' mistakes, and that agents on one machine share its user account, so the machine is the hard boundary (web/shell/src/people/model.ts:10-11, spec 2026-10-08 §6.8). Evidence: shell/src/people PersonCard and People tests pass (24 tests), e2e/people.spec.ts passes, and the owner's raise panel and the person's narrow panel were checked in a browser at 1280 and 390 px, light and dark.","supersedes":"d00b8522e108554edd0dbdc2179840a7a8bee0f5ab73d0f2c6417287c6e91721","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:13:39.984919Z","id":"63d5333b003a91abb762e33d76dc2ec341d1b6df3c4f49e36a487c130890b862","body":{"detail":"machineCaps/agentCaps treat a capability as on when any access object of its type grants the action anywhere, and narrowGrant/narrowAgent build a narrowing as the person's rights less whole actions. A narrowing made outside People (location-limited, from a script) shows as fully on for an action it grants at one artifact, and an agent narrowing built on such a machine narrowing can be refused 400 not_narrower (shown as the daemon words it). No route makes location-limited narrowings today besides direct API calls.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":74},"end":{"line":116},"content_hash":"94fa9f9f7aaec826bea13c4880fbd5d2110d4970ca56dd0c16c9d2303deba841"},"summary":"People reads and builds narrowings by whole actions, ignoring locations","supersedes":"d3a77187ab40c8951702a77e1abda27f00151bdb12ac792b53b4970bfc03cb73","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:13:39.987900Z","id":"105dca3f42db934c6f63540c127899ec78de6d01447f3ebf5ba8f071c17612cb","body":{"detail":"Spec section 3.4's example raises an agent for one artifact (Publish versions of \"Quarterly Review\"). People raises an action at \"*\" only, which keeps the panel to one list of checkboxes; the route takes locations, so a per-artifact raise is a UI addition.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":121},"end":{"line":135},"content_hash":"6149476116b6fdf827b3dd235aa856cc5f10de23b97a42e122f6bb285bb4a081"},"summary":"Raises are at every artifact; no per-artifact raise in People","supersedes":"9b37d8dce5820c899da52cf299a93663649f27a8c6418a23c977dea3bd3d52e6","tags":["revisit:the owner asks to raise an agent for one artifact","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/PersonCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:10:34.936872Z","id":"729d67459f045beef7e0d47841d31563e02f1682fdb95257f46b3014d96db86b","body":{"detail":"The owner's answer: on a person's card the install owner also sees that person's live approvals whose author is the owner (approvals covering the owner's content); a person's approvals of others' content stay private to them. Spec decision O12, sections 9.5, 17 and 18.","kind":"comment","references":"1b80cc4d5ab2c276004f0603af7967360282105d186ad37cc3da1cc93ebda9f3","span":{"start":{"line":241},"end":{"line":248},"content_hash":"9ca48a48ef707b2f209861bc8a887915d841705e8943e97a154d3783b54584d5"},"summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-13): \"Your content only\": the owner reads a person's approvals of the owner's content, and no other approval of theirs","tags":["status:decided","owner-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/PersonCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:10:35.646293Z","id":"cd8df61f83f9588caa4b3a7f750065485793e068d2991b94d27a8c125182a52e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5c7597dc","summary":"Fixed as the owner decided (\"Your content only\"): GET /api/people carries each person's live approvals of the owner's content (approvals_of_yours, crates/clax-server/src/routes/people.rs), and the owner's card shows them read-only under \"Approvals of your content\" (PersonCard.svelte:241-248, its own part since 4248defd). Evidence: cargo nextest run -p clax-server --test integration -E 'test(the_owner_sees_exactly_a_persons_approvals_of_the_owners_content)' passes (Sam's approval of Mia stays out, Mia reads none of Sam's); npx vitest run shell/src/people passes ('shows the owner the person's approvals of the owner's content, read-only'); npx playwright test e2e/creator-raise.spec.ts passes (Sam's card reads 'Allowed everywhere').","supersedes":"1b80cc4d5ab2c276004f0603af7967360282105d186ad37cc3da1cc93ebda9f3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/PersonCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:05:59.886354Z","id":"25d4e5e7d352e21878cf431ccdbdccbfcb03ca10dd01166dda89b455a4385499","body":{"detail":"raiseCaps (web/shell/src/people/model.ts) marks a capability `on` when the owner's elevation raises it, and enabled when the agent's rights without the elevation lack it. Since 'Narrowing caps raises' (spec §7.2, rights::cap_raise), an action the person holds and the agent's or machine's narrowing turns off is off for every raise. Observed: Mia narrowed notes-fix without Delete; the owner's panel on Mia's card showed 'Delete artifacts' checked and enabled, and the summary 'Raise this agent (raised)', while the agent's effective rights had no delete anywhere. The person's view gained the note 'but off while this is off'; the owner's has nothing, so the owner can raise an action that does nothing and believe it took.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":230},"end":{"line":232},"content_hash":"d08eb17de349fd3115cc0e447414ed3cad0ac97d4717803fe3b540aabaaa54cd"},"suggested_fix":"In raiseCaps, mark a capability the person holds and a narrowing (agent's or machine's) turns off as capped, and show it as off with a note such as 'off while their narrowing turns it off'.","summary":"The owner's Raise this agent panel shows a raise the agent's narrowing caps as on, with no note","tags":["review","ui","t20b-rereview","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/PersonCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:05:59.886391Z","id":"46f31f1d51671d9676a8fff9e763b19941ef64d2a18ea9a6bfdc2522861f06b0","body":{"detail":"creatorRaise maps an access with no locations (clax-ask) to '*', so the raise line reads 'Raised by the owner until this session ends: ..., Ask questions on every artifact'. clax-ask has no location (spec §7.1, rights.rs RightType::located); the checkbox note elsewhere says just 'Raised by the owner'. Seen on Mia's People at 1280 and 390 px.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":69},"end":{"line":70},"content_hash":"73d4a8cc3301c1c740969a75d08ebe4ec6175bf84342d64a6cd3098bb41380b5"},"suggested_fix":"For a location-less access, render the label alone ('Ask questions').","summary":"A raise line names an owner's ask raise as 'Ask questions on every artifact'","tags":["review","ui","t20b-rereview","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/PersonCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:02:24.343218Z","id":"4f6bfa3099946bfb0436bb4a96e52e0aa0fa0b643f29f1a4b007d59388858fbf","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:702d726c","summary":"Fixed: raiseCaps (web/shell/src/people/model.ts) marks capped a capability the agent's or its machine's narrowing turns off; the owner's Raise this agent panel shows 'Off by <person>'s narrowing: a raise gives nothing while it is off' beside it and disables it unless it is raised (so a raise can still be dropped). Evidence: PersonCard.test.ts 'marks in the owner's raise panel what the agent's narrowing turns off' passes; the mutation capped: false fails it.","supersedes":"25d4e5e7d352e21878cf431ccdbdccbfcb03ca10dd01166dda89b455a4385499","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/PersonCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:02:24.344186Z","id":"b51638fcc508d6612b794ce8b0171fd58770a14c330295754e5b5fce94604ac1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:702d726c","summary":"Fixed: PersonCard.svelte names a raised capability through raisedAs, which gives clax-ask no place: 'Ask questions', not 'on every artifact', in both the owner's raise list and the raise lines. Evidence: PersonCard.test.ts 'marks in the owner's raise panel ... and names a raised ask without a place' passes (.raises reads 'Ask questions'; Mia's raise line reads 'Raised by Mia until this session ends: Ask questions').","supersedes":"46f31f1d51671d9676a8fff9e763b19941ef64d2a18ea9a6bfdc2522861f06b0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/AgentStrip.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T22:24:19.594288Z","id":"d112f1c6a32200d35eecb57274b6237cfb708027f50fc23217259a9325ebf3a3","body":{"detail":"The strip and the artifact's People panel say \"quarterly-fix-chart · waiting on you 56 min (1 approval)\" when the only open request is a routing one (Mia sent a thread to it); GET /api/agents gives that agent state \"idle\" (crates/clax-server/src/routes/people.rs:176 makes `waiting` only for a question or a `cause: ask` request). The agent never asked and is not waiting. The owner's People panel also says \"sam-notes · Waiting on Sam 30 min (1 approval)\" while Mia's panel reads the same agent as \"Idle.\". Spec 2026-10-08 §13 defines waiting as an open question or ask request.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":20},"end":{"line":25},"content_hash":"6f155ee0207dd085ff14bc59659086a355c4406191f9e83fcab8f9d5d38933da"},"suggested_fix":"Word a routing hold as \"1 approval for you\" (or \"held: 1 approval\") rather than \"waiting on you\", and keep \"waiting\" for state = waiting.","summary":"\"Waiting on you\" for an agent whose state is idle: routing requests count as a block, and viewers disagree","tags":["review","final-review-ui","wording","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/AgentStrip.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T22:24:19.594373Z","id":"e08d3df3aeb612e5f477dbc435b6b22ed27db24e1e29d464b291cbe7270111e1","body":{"detail":"With Sam's agent `sam-notes` and the owner's agents in the owner's strip, the chip reads \"sam-notes · 2 unread\" with no \"· Sam\", where the owner chip, the Send menu and the People panel all say \"sam-notes · Sam\" / \"Sam's agent\". Spec 2026-10-08 §11 Display: agents show with their person wherever more than one person's agents appear.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":23},"end":{"line":23},"content_hash":"bcfe179fa2445e69a8743858eb888accb82f3a73caa0ed331158b6ab39128e59"},"summary":"The owner's agent strip names another person's agent without its person","tags":["review","final-review-ui","naming","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/People.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T22:24:19.594403Z","id":"fd0926fa81d6836358b5354b876dde182cab062f26220c9d708c4441afa8e1cc","body":{"detail":"The owner's PersonCard (PersonCard.svelte:256) links each waiting request to its inbox card; a connected person's own People lists theirs as a div with no link, so Sam cannot get from People to the decision. Both say \"1 from Mia for sam-notes\" with no noun; the inbox says \"1 comment on Quarterly Review\".","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":190},"end":{"line":193},"content_hash":"2a7e30edeb7ad593e59393a3d911e96a25c30e7f8f2ba1f969f5ac5ae1c9e29b"},"summary":"A person's own \"Waiting\" rows are plain text, not links, and read \"1 from Mia for sam-notes\"","tags":["review","final-review-ui","wording","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/People.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T22:24:19.594558Z","id":"66cbecfc6a2549fa6636ec82598ae55371ead1cc5d2292b5b43545fb5fd7895f","body":{"detail":"A LAN viewer at /people reads \"only the owner or a connected person has People\"; a person whose People was open when the owner revoked them reads the same, with no word that they were disconnected. The connection card shows \"that is not the request's code\" and \"the name 'Аlex' is taken\" for a Cyrillic look-alike (it is not taken, it looks like the owner's).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":130},"end":{"line":130},"content_hash":"9351beb2d7ddbe6086dcf1d96e3f91fd362f287dd44b1cf91f95ca4de3c2a137"},"summary":"Daemon refusals show raw as the page's text: lower-case, no full stop, and a revoked person is not told why","tags":["review","final-review-ui","wording","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/AgentStrip.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T03:13:17.311784Z","id":"eab31497509e89bd8a9725567b6d344cb96c4d422f89036ae6a83faa90ddbb9f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:07908a6b","summary":"The strip says 'waiting on you' only with an open question; approval requests alone read '1 approval for you · <time>'. The People panel says an agent waits only when GET /api/agents gives state 'waiting', so every viewer reads the same; approvals alone waiting on you say so. Evidence: AgentStrip.test.ts and people-panel.test.ts pass; Chromium: the owner's panel reads 'sam-notes · Sam Idle.' while Sam's strip reads 'sam-notes · 1 approval for you · under a minute'.","supersedes":"d112f1c6a32200d35eecb57274b6237cfb708027f50fc23217259a9325ebf3a3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/AgentStrip.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T03:13:17.313644Z","id":"45dfdaf5a8cf9582ea27af8cbbe2062b6ec5eff42b76a3f511d435fdf90bf128","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:07908a6b","summary":"GET /api/inbox?group=agent carries person, person_name and own (crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs strip_view, AgentGroup.person); the chip names another person's agent with its person. Evidence: AgentStrip.test.ts 'names another person's agent with its person...' and api_agents::roster_reports_blocked_since_and_is_person_scoped pass; Chromium: the owner's strip reads 'sam-notes · Sam · 1 unread'.","supersedes":"e08d3df3aeb612e5f477dbc435b6b22ed27db24e1e29d464b291cbe7270111e1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/People.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T03:13:17.319008Z","id":"bf4d3149af634229d7d4836a8a0a856172d56d68ac78d55a86f3732743102db1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2eb5ce4a","summary":"A person's Waiting rows link to /inbox?approval=<id> and read '1 comment from Mia for sam-notes' (waitText in people/model.ts, shared with PersonCard). Evidence: People.test.ts passes; Chromium as Sam: [A, '1 comment from Mia for sam-notes', '/inbox?approval=…'].","supersedes":"fd0926fa81d6836358b5354b876dde182cab062f26220c9d708c4441afa8e1cc","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/People.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T03:13:17.320826Z","id":"b8ab0eae04b2b6dd86bfba3b903c87a8dc746acc2c2db815333383928f73ac6e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2eb5ce4a","summary":"people/refusal.ts words name_taken, invalid_name and wrong_code, makes any other refusal a sentence, and says why People is not this browser's: never connected, or disconnected by the owner. Evidence: refusal.test.ts, People.test.ts, people.spec.ts pass; Chromium: a LAN viewer reads 'People is for the owner of this Clax and the people they connect. To connect, ask the owner for an invite.'; Sam, revoked with People open, reads 'You are no longer connected: the owner disconnected you. Ask them for a new invite to connect again.'","supersedes":"66cbecfc6a2549fa6636ec82598ae55371ead1cc5d2292b5b43545fb5fd7895f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"2694e017ce4028b717ae68cea620f160781dbbbfd133b686a58e032eb76fb88a","body":{"detail":"raiseCaps tests the unraised rights at the artifact's ID, and an `own` location never covers a bare artifact ID (narrowerOrEqual's within). People does not know which artifacts are the person's (the artifact list carries no creator person), so for a Collaborator's agent 'Publish new versions' and 'Delete artifacts' at one of the person's own artifacts show unchecked and raisable. Raising there adds nothing the agent lacked; it only says less than it could. Fixing it needs the artifacts' person in GET /api/artifacts or a per-artifact rights check route.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":141},"end":{"line":158},"content_hash":"2920b50211feb7bfd4fc12cf7f96d2345f50abb8a6b0e84b4167a6d1e2dc53df"},"summary":"A raise at one of the person's own artifacts shows as not held","supersedes":"d9c7672405a3113bea7e8664d0b72679c446253cbd106d534da3e9da67f5156a","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
