{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/People.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:31:12.225249Z","id":"fefac2072dd866b39f6936bcc2cc785d2a9cea5f4227284fe9c2577237f0bad0","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"c819019969a294866a5bb1d07c1dba5094d684ed7fde22cef3fb9e2074cd6d3e","summary":"Duplicate head left by a merge: this is a parallel branch's re-anchor of the record that b714cf82b695aa82d6ba568c91acfba8af3a5186a181207c3f81361488bb95bd closed (The inbox's connection card approves a request with its code, a new person's name and a preset (web/shell/src/people/ConnectionCard.svelte). Evidence: npx vites). That close stands in the merged code; this head carries no new content. Proposed close: reason:duplicate.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:34:33.800076Z","id":"e2981b5fdea740ebbd5a677453a22dc70466eb3ac4fdd53a06ab5562494224db","body":{"detail":"machineCaps/agentCaps treat a capability as on when any access object of its type grants the action anywhere, and narrowGrant/narrowAgent build a narrowing as the person's rights less whole actions. A narrowing made outside People (location-limited, from a script) shows as fully on for an action it grants at one artifact, and an agent narrowing built on such a machine narrowing can be refused 400 not_narrower (shown as the daemon words it). No route makes location-limited narrowings today besides direct API calls.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":70},"end":{"line":91},"content_hash":"99b719adf2022cceb41bb99664443e891a3471d15932bb0a42ccbd9dc5e3c851"},"summary":"People reads and builds narrowings by whole actions, ignoring locations","supersedes":"63d5333b003a91abb762e33d76dc2ec341d1b6df3c4f49e36a487c130890b862","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/InviteDialog.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:23.182808Z","id":"aa1e7141638bd656e79bd857f8786f5c7f88d2e060bf7de7b29fbc417d7e6e2b","body":{"detail":"POST /api/people/invites takes {viewer} (spec section 6.2), but the dialog offers only a new person or the owner's own machine. Naming a new person after a viewer who was never invited is 409 name_taken, whose message says to invite that viewer, which People cannot do yet. A viewer picker would use GET /api/viewers?q=.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":77},"end":{"line":78},"content_hash":"5aed600e45e79d959736f2f8b5fad319e35a36576ba1a9b733b99cfe892345cf"},"summary":"No invite for an existing LAN viewer","supersedes":"7519ac056bc8df461d5a3df7a41594fcfae082a4a7ed907afecfd183ec6ecf88","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/People.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:23.197853Z","id":"cc7345965db0aa668018eee20cd421dcff8756ff54aaf019dc90c536ada33889","body":{"detail":"People lists pending requests with Deny and links to the inbox for Approve; the approve form (code, new name, preset) is the inbox's connection card, which plan Task 21 builds (web/shell/src/people/ConnectionCard.svelte). Until then the inbox shows the request but cannot approve it from the shell.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":160},"end":{"line":160},"content_hash":"6a6b23888f43df54bf7304ec4eb8761e91735497209e0e4775466d231db404a7"},"summary":"Connection requests are approved in the inbox, not on People","supersedes":"c819019969a294866a5bb1d07c1dba5094d684ed7fde22cef3fb9e2074cd6d3e","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:23.212096Z","id":"cf305e78e781c7e0223f920de37fb986e43afb347ef4e80115445f5d0d5a85b6","body":{"detail":"machineCaps/agentCaps treat a capability as on when any access object of its type grants the action anywhere, and narrowGrant/narrowAgent build a narrowing as the person's rights less whole actions. A narrowing made outside People (location-limited, from a script) shows as fully on for an action it grants at one artifact, and an agent narrowing built on such a machine narrowing can be refused 400 not_narrower (shown as the daemon words it). No route makes location-limited narrowings today besides direct API calls.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":71},"end":{"line":92},"content_hash":"99b719adf2022cceb41bb99664443e891a3471d15932bb0a42ccbd9dc5e3c851"},"summary":"People reads and builds narrowings by whole actions, ignoring locations","supersedes":"e2981b5fdea740ebbd5a677453a22dc70466eb3ac4fdd53a06ab5562494224db","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/People.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T15:56:02.498142Z","id":"d5134bbe473d262ed3ed13b4457611055d8d5ada604c08c2ea62ad55bec2f2f8","body":{"detail":"People starts import(\"../hosted/HostedPanel.svelte\") beside its GET /api/hosted/me, so a hosted page waits on no extra round trip; a local daemon's /people fetches the chunk (HostedPanel, about 4 KB gzip) and never mounts it. Starting the import only after /api/hosted/me answers with a person would spare local daemons the fetch but put a round trip before the hosted panel shows.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":128},"end":{"line":137},"content_hash":"6ffb4a26ed16809a3bbe650c858092c02f8336048c37d8f20846da36f2198ee9"},"summary":"HostedPanel's chunk loads only once GET /api/hosted/me says the daemon is hosted","tags":["bundle","hosted","revisit:the shell knows at boot whether its daemon is hosted (a flag in the page) before People's first request","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/People.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T16:45:12.319309Z","id":"c1c78f7c883117600c070d49bc2dfd0776c6ece8aeaf4964f6673eb6459989f2","body":{"detail":"Moved from web/shell/src/people/People.svelte:160, record cc734596.\n\nPeople lists pending requests with Deny and links to the inbox for Approve; the approve form (code, new name, preset) is the inbox's connection card, which plan Task 21 builds (web/shell/src/people/ConnectionCard.svelte). Until then the inbox shows the request but cannot approve it from the shell.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":171},"end":{"line":171},"content_hash":"6a6b23888f43df54bf7304ec4eb8761e91735497209e0e4775466d231db404a7"},"summary":"Connection requests are approved in the inbox, not on People","supersedes":"cc7345965db0aa668018eee20cd421dcff8756ff54aaf019dc90c536ada33889","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/ApprovalCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:19:43.039973Z","id":"106d2029062da810c76fde7cf5e7ce6ee4db6a16baaefc7e099283a0e7d1d4f3","body":{"detail":"Comments are rendered as Markdown (web/shell/src/view/markdown.ts) and previews elsewhere show them without syntax (view/md-load.svelte.ts plainText). Approving decides what reaches an agent, which reads the raw text, so this card keeps the raw text: syntax that renders as nothing cannot hide words from the approver. The renderer already shows link reference definitions and over-nested bodies as text, so the stripped text would hold the same words; showing it stripped is a one-line change (plainText(x.body)). Which the approver should see is the owner's call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":45},"end":{"line":45},"content_hash":"77ded58e81c9f34af3eec71ec339cbb6c55f2a8146d83e9ee8d849122a0413fa"},"summary":"Approval requests show the withheld comments exactly as written, not with Markdown syntax taken away like the other previews","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/ApprovalCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:04:26.800192Z","id":"9c4ddc74a85514c9c0fdbd5f1fd6c1433baf45b43970253fb9bfca87af632f17","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:04af9d60f","summary":"Withheld comments render as Markdown (ui/Markdown.svelte) under their author, first three lines until Show all; the renderer shows the whole comment as text when a reading would drop a word. Tests: web/shell/src/people/ApprovalCard.test.ts 'ApprovalCard's comments as Markdown' (a reference definition's title, raw HTML and an image's alt all show), web/e2e/inbox-cards.spec.ts (bazelisk test //web:unit and //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--grep='decides an approval', both pass).","supersedes":"106d2029062da810c76fde7cf5e7ce6ee4db6a16baaefc7e099283a0e7d1d4f3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/People.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:49:54.136800Z","id":"939c064f5e1e3c24656a045971ca24eeff0fab0092a836fbc7beca68fa5fcfda","body":{"detail":"approvals.filter(a => a.author.public_id === p.public_id) groups by listed people; remote-author approvals made since a1f58e923 match none. The inbox approval card (ApprovalCard.svelte) shows and decides them, and DELETE /api/approvals/{id} revokes them, but no page lists them for the owner. A 'People on other Clax' card listing the leftovers would close it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":190},"end":{"line":190},"content_hash":"0ebd44595066b4ddfa33e163a7461112640e99098dec6b911e8df03a64f5b965"},"summary":"The owner's People page lists approvals and waiting requests only under connected people, so an approval of a hosted author (remote:<origin>#<ID>) shows nowhere there and cannot be revoked from People","tags":["ui","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/People.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:35:54.411935Z","id":"ed5e83203a4e6d4a34def57800f52a8fe26efce1dba1dfa1b37974d6eec42355","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:eb463b678","summary":"The owner's People page has a 'People on other Clax' card listing approvals and open requests whose author key starts remote:, by the name the daemon gives (crates/clax-http/src/views/approval.rs person(): '<name> (on <remote>)'), never the key, with Revoke (DELETE /api/approvals/<id>). Test 'shows the owner the people on other Clax they approved, by name, with Revoke, and what waits on them' (web/shell/src/people/People.test.ts); //web:unit passes. Mutation: the old People.svelte fails it.","supersedes":"939c064f5e1e3c24656a045971ca24eeff0fab0092a836fbc7beca68fa5fcfda","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/People.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:50:56.443160Z","id":"231b9dc0e58f598ff92d6f09003f402444b7cccf1caf24ef4e3e739e31e5dae1","body":{"detail":"People starts import(\"../hosted/HostedPanel.svelte\") beside its GET /api/hosted/me, so a hosted page waits on no extra round trip; a local daemon's /people fetches the chunk (HostedPanel, about 4 KB gzip) and never mounts it. Starting the import only after /api/hosted/me answers with a person would spare local daemons the fetch but put a round trip before the hosted panel shows.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":131},"end":{"line":141},"content_hash":"58a26e3234a2d048edefb8e3bb50350322f7709b8b234fb1ce14f4ca704aff6b"},"summary":"HostedPanel's chunk loads only once GET /api/hosted/me says the daemon is hosted","supersedes":"d5134bbe473d262ed3ed13b4457611055d8d5ada604c08c2ea62ad55bec2f2f8","tags":["bundle","hosted","revisit:the shell knows at boot whether its daemon is hosted (a flag in the page) before People's first request","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/People.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:50:56.473208Z","id":"a3686175332de2b5f1176d4cd0d55a16fbe7c40cb6179e6ea23d4ac0f6e15964","body":{"detail":"Moved from web/shell/src/people/People.svelte:160, record cc734596.\n\nPeople lists pending requests with Deny and links to the inbox for Approve; the approve form (code, new name, preset) is the inbox's connection card, which plan Task 21 builds (web/shell/src/people/ConnectionCard.svelte). Until then the inbox shows the request but cannot approve it from the shell.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":176},"end":{"line":176},"content_hash":"6a6b23888f43df54bf7304ec4eb8761e91735497209e0e4775466d231db404a7"},"summary":"Connection requests are approved in the inbox, not on People","supersedes":"c1c78f7c883117600c070d49bc2dfd0776c6ece8aeaf4964f6673eb6459989f2","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/PersonCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:45.983469Z","id":"0e6ccf2aa6aab3070b5b78966143eec9bc593b971c09d0900d981a25185a90c6","body":{"detail":"The owner's answer: on a person's card the install owner also sees that person's live approvals whose author is the owner (approvals covering the owner's content); a person's approvals of others' content stay private to them. Spec decision O12, sections 9.5, 17 and 18.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from web/shell/src/people/PersonCard.svelte:241:248 to web/shell/src/people/PersonCard.svelte:272:279: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"comment","references":"cd8df61f83f9588caa4b3a7f750065485793e068d2991b94d27a8c125182a52e","span":{"start":{"line":272},"end":{"line":279},"content_hash":"9ca48a48ef707b2f209861bc8a887915d841705e8943e97a154d3783b54584d5"},"summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-13): \"Your content only\": the owner reads a person's approvals of the owner's content, and no other approval of theirs","supersedes":"729d67459f045beef7e0d47841d31563e02f1682fdb95257f46b3014d96db86b","tags":["status:decided","owner-decision","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/api.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T05:25:49.588191Z","id":"030312d9a0ca5e42bb5f1e1f6e631d1333e2c554f22ee56a4cb44fe7827988ea","body":{"detail":"The branch adds two new copies of people/api.ts's call() (q/remote-api.ts:9-15, almost character for character, and q/passkey.ts:65-75 with a confirmation header and a new PasskeyRefused class), plus hand-written fetch/parse/throw in q/confirm.svelte.ts:37-57 with a third new error class, ConfirmRefused, of the same shape (status, message, code) as people/api.ts's Refused and api.ts's ApiError. It also pastes the same three lines `const held = await heldOf(res); if (held) throw new X(202, held.message, HELD);` into people/api.ts:20, hosted/api.ts:52, q/api.ts:22 and ui/publish-api.ts:55. The cost already shows: remote-api.ts is the one copy that missed the held check (see the blocker on web/shell/src/q/remote-api.ts:9-26), and callers have to know which class a module throws (refusal() in people/refusal.ts reads `code` from any of them; ConfirmationCard and PasskeySettings print e.message instead).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":17},"end":{"line":25},"content_hash":"c33e2ccce471ccabfae7b1f1f846929b1271e4744cf7c181919914897b2b88c1"},"suggested_fix":"Export one `browserCall<T>(path, {method, body, headers})` from a small shared module (e.g. web/shell/src/held.ts, or a new web/shell/src/browser-api.ts beside it) that does the fetch, the heldOf check, the 204 and JSON handling, and throws people/api.ts's Refused (status, message, code, plus `held` when 202). Have people/api.ts, hosted/api.ts, q/remote-api.ts, q/passkey.ts (passing its x-clax-confirmation header) and q/confirm.svelte.ts call it, and delete PasskeyRefused and ConfirmRefused. q/api.ts and ui/publish-api.ts, which throw ApiError and use the token, can share the same held check through one helper rather than their own copies.","summary":"The shell now has six copies of the same cookie fetch wrapper, each with its own error class, and the branch threads the held-confirmation check into each one by hand","tags":["review","review:ri-quality","duplication","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/api.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T05:30:17.462043Z","id":"bbc9ffb17aca4dc6738b90e5b105b1975bbeb51e1182a7cbd2b8cc84c15a164c","body":{"detail":"Same fetch/held/ok/parse/throw shape in web/shell/src/people/api.ts:17-26, hosted/api.ts:49-57, q/remote-api.ts:9-15 (no held check), q/passkey.ts:65-75 (PasskeyRefused), q/confirm.svelte.ts:29-57 (ConfirmRefused with the same status/message/code fields as people/api.ts Refused). The three-line heldOf/throw block appears at people/api.ts:20-21, hosted/api.ts:52-53, q/api.ts:22-23, ui/publish-api.ts:55-56, q/passkey.ts:69-70. The merge is workable: passkey.ts differs only by the optional confirmation header; q/api.ts (403 -> forbidden, 409 closed) and publish-api.ts (token, ApiError) are already scoped by the suggested fix to sharing just the held check.","kind":"comment","references":"030312d9a0ca5e42bb5f1e1f6e631d1333e2c554f22ee56a4cb44fe7827988ea","summary":"confirmed: the cookie fetch wrapper and its error class are copied across the shell, with the held check pasted into each","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/people/api.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T06:03:23.720916Z","id":"dbb8b74d0bb2e75b8578755e99da35aa40ac673dc54111cc08d84cf127dfe519","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b5e17a7a0","summary":"people/api.ts, hosted/api.ts, q/remote-api.ts, q/passkey.ts and q/confirm.svelte.ts call held.ts browserCall (fetch, held check, 204/JSON, Refused with `held`); PasskeyRefused and ConfirmRefused are deleted and bot/api.ts takes Refused from held.ts. q/api.ts and ui/publish-api.ts keep their token/ApiError wrappers with the two-line heldOf check, and queues/api.ts its own Refused (no held decisions). bazelisk test //web:unit //web:typecheck //web:lint pass (held.test.ts, passkey.test.ts, confirmation-card.test.ts, refusal.test.ts).","supersedes":"030312d9a0ca5e42bb5f1e1f6e631d1333e2c554f22ee56a4cb44fe7827988ea","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
